the same for the same system, and `archimedeanTruncatedCuboctahedron_nu_reps` the statement in Mathlib's terms alone (`IsPolyRootEq`):
`ν Archimedean.TruncatedCuboctahedron.polyhedron` is the first coordinate of the root of each of these systems, each with exactly one root in its
box; it implies `IsPolyRootMax` (`IsPolyRootEq.isPolyRootMax`). There is one system (`PolynomialSystem.IsRootMax.isRootEq_singleton`).
Generated by `lean/scripts/exact_n.py` from the theorems of `Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandArchimedeanTruncatedCuboctahedron`, `Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandArchimedeanTruncatedCuboctahedron.Exact` and
`Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandArchimedeanTruncatedCuboctahedron.Roots`, which it does not change.
-/

